6f01039313b46935bcf90bee118dad4bd074214","fulfillmentEvidence":{"actorInvocationRef":"actor-invocation://abiogenesis/1fef0e0deb9fd1547c4a1a136b87efd8eb9439a12c8cad4083156b9d77805693","assessmentContractRef":null,"cCallRef":"c-call:sha256:8cb536ba40931799b9f3d05c06f01039313b46935bcf90bee118dad4bd074214","commands":[],"contractRef":"contract://abiogenesis/worksite/native-work/observation@5","dependencies":[{"digest":"sha256:fe8f40803a256b5b65c97f5f4cae862fd55b37cb81f2a803c56c3f654c22e9ef","path":"generated/hello-world.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:028073e4cb24bd7444dd15d48b0e16d37df236edf7a003cb3ca26286aca6c585","path":"source/basic-cli.oracle.json"},{"digest":"sha256:ce602ce2cc0fcefaba288623a675a770d11bc14d224b90045aebbe031330172f","path":"source/original-basic-cli.txt"},{"digest":"sha256:f97359de0fe6181e44c334496993b20b82b49cdbbf0b8b66ee18de7eac34a63b","path":"source/witness-contract.md"},{"digest":"sha256:9d02e5fb3f2793e187a7afa673594340a8cb311d6e212cd3b77ba1a764eb43ee","path":"specification/project-conformance.md"},{"digest":"sha256:8b55bf3f6324da565a1de9a5186444e36c43f450484463aafc84b65fd9da4613","path":"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:5449c227c7173bb1b812e46e06d3341b1624e832a2a74105f9a109ee201134d4","path":"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs"}],"files":[{"digest":"sha256:fe8f40803a256b5b65c97f5f4cae862fd55b37cb81f2a803c56c3f654c22e9ef","path":"generated/hello-world.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:028073e4cb24bd7444dd15d48b0e16d37df236edf7a003cb3ca26286aca6c585","path":"source/basic-cli.oracle.json"},{"digest":"sha256:ce602ce2cc0fcefaba288623a675a770d11bc14d224b90045aebbe031330172f","path":"source/original-basic-cli.txt"},{"digest":"sha256:f97359de0fe6181e44c334496993b20b82b49cdbbf0b8b66ee18de7eac34a63b","path":"source/witness-contract.md"},{"digest":"sha256:9d02e5fb3f2793e187a7afa673594340a8cb311d6e212cd3b77ba1a764eb43ee","path":"specification/project-conformance.md"},{"digest":"sha256:8b55bf3f6324da565a1de9a5186444e36c43f450484463aafc84b65fd9da4613","path":"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:5449c227c7173bb1b812e46e06d3341b1624e832a2a74105f9a109ee201134d4","path":"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs"}],"kind":"native","producerActorRef":null,"producerResultRef":null,"resultDigest":"sha256:33db8d198f2a1114256e2cda6fb6ed740af20bc95de2a7c8bb44ee1dcff12b08","resultRef":"result://abiogenesis/33db8d198f2a1114256e2cda6fb6ed740af20bc95de2a7c8bb44ee1dcff12b08"},"purpose":"specification","resultDigest":"sha256:33db8d198f2a1114256e2cda6fb6ed740af20bc95de2a7c8bb44ee1dcff12b08","resultRef":"result://abiogenesis/33db8d198f2a1114256e2cda6fb6ed740af20bc95de2a7c8bb44ee1dcff12b08","selectedGraphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/specification@5","synthesisResultRef":"result://abiogenesis/a5bb14481704b1846a3ec5fcc21cf3a8eab60d52f9e009ea1c0dd40fd373b3ae","value":{"changedPaths":["specification/project-conformance.md"],"report":{"gaps":["The conformance obligation is not closed: this document still needs recorded evidence of this write and an independent assessment by a different actor/call. My own reading is not acceptance.","`design/implementation-design.md` and `design/test-design.md` are still missing (both the `design/` directory and the files). Both are outside my write scope. The implementation-design and test-design obligations stay open.","`test-execution-plan.json` is still missing and outside my write scope. The execution-plan obligation stays open. How it should encode the direct CLI command (`node generated/hello-world.mjs`) is an open choice (U-5).","The behavior and revision obligations have baseline and post-fix command evidence on CLI fe8f4080…. Whether that evidence is current and correctly paired is for the runtime to compute. Both obligations still need the independent assessment.","The complete-original obligation stays open until all four written assets exist and the independent assessment has accepted current evidence.","Unresolved unknowns: the Node version is not in the recorded evidence (U-1); the source does not constrain stderr (U-2); arguments, stdin and running from another directory are unspecified (U-3); only one macOS host is evidenced (U-4).","Not an unscoped write, but disclosed: writing the document also created the `specification/` directory, since the file's parent did not exist. I used pipes only to compute the expected output's SHA-256 and created no temporary files."],"summary":"I wrote `specification/project-conformance.md` (sha256 9d02e5fb…43ee). No other file was changed. Writing it created the parent `specification/` directory, which did not exist before; that directory is the only side effect of this write. I did not run either fixed command.\n\nWhat the document covers:\n- **Intent and scope:** the Intent of the basic-cli task, the product (`generated/hello-world.mjs`, run as `node generated/hello-world.mjs` from the project root with no arguments), the two supplied tests and the test command, what is out of scope, and which files are protected or writable.\n- **Stage table:** all 8 original stages, each saying whether its file is authored here, supplied, reused, corrected, or carried by recorded command evidence.\n- **Requirements R-01..R-14:** each cites the original source (by stage), the oracle, or the witness contract. The key ones:\n  - stdout is exactly `Hello, world!\\n` (14 bytes, hex and SHA-256 given; I recomputed the digest through a pipe and it matches the recorded run).\n  - exit status is 0, with no package installation.\n  - both tests use `node:test`, `node:assert/strict` and `spawnSync`, run the real CLI from the project root, and assert status 0 and the exact stdout.\n  - the test run has at least 2 passes and 0 failures, with at least one pass from each test file (a pass count alone is not enough).\n  - the fields `test-execution-plan.json` must contain, what the two design documents must contain, the baseline-then-fix history, and the write limits.\n- **Acceptance criteria AC-01..AC-12:** each has a decidable pass rule, including the original \"accept only if\" rule for the test result (exit 0, observed passes ≥ expected, plan satisfied).\n- **Oracle mapping:** every oracle field is traced to a requirement or criterion.\n\nConflicts I kept visible rather than resolving silently:\n- **C-1:** the original asks for a handwritten `test-execution-result.json`. The witness contract confines writes to other paths and requires recorded command evidence instead, and the oracle does not list the file. I kept the file's meaning and assigned it to the recorded evidence.\n- **C-2:** the original says the worker runs the tests itself. The witness contract says an author's own report is not evidence.\n- **C-3:** the original stage order versus the CLI and tests being supplied up front.\n- **C-4:** `assertedReturnValue` is `\"Hello, world!\"` while stdout is `\"Hello, world!\\n\"`. These are consistent and neither should be \"normalized\" into the other.\n- **C-5:** the UAT stage only asks for an output check, but the test-design stage requires status 0 too.\n- **C-6:** the conformance stage wording mentions only stdout.\n- **C-7:** the supplied CLI did not conform.\n\nUnknowns U-1..U-6: Node version, stderr, other invocations, line endings on other platforms, how the plan should encode the direct CLI command, and the library's internal mechanics.\n\nSection 7 records the recorded history, tied to exact file hashes and marked as information only, not acceptance:\n- **Baseline run** (result 6514754a, CLI 647697a5): the CLI printed `Hello world!\\n` without the comma, and the tests exited 1 with 0 passes and 2 failures.\n- **One-line fix** (result e897db22): the CLI's hash changed to fe8f4080.\n- **Run after the fix** (result db34d3cf): the CLI printed `Hello, world!\\n` and exited 0, and the tests exited 0 with 2 passes and 0 failures.\n\nThe baseline failure stays attached to the old bytes. I re-checked the hashes: the original source, oracle, witness contract, both test files and the current CLI (fe8f4080…) all match their recorded values."}}},{"actorInvocationRef":"actor-invocation://abiogenesis/9fb67c0ad7be41b7d9d91e06599dd885e7cc99d0a511ecfa4666583a4365145d","cCallRef":"c-call:sha256:b3edbe60907190e33d3c78a3e3aaedeaaf16d7fb1dbd47a7b4530dfb0aa53b61","fulfillmentEvidence":{"actorInvocationRef":"actor-invocation://abiogenesis/9fb67c0ad7be41b7d9d91e06599dd885e7cc99d0a511ecfa4666583a4365145d","assessmentContractRef":null,"cCallRef":"c-call:sha256:b3edbe60907190e33d3c78a3e3aaedeaaf16d7fb1dbd47a7b4530dfb0aa53b61","commands":[],"contractRef":"contract://abiogenesis/worksite/native-work/observation@5","dependencies":[{"digest":"sha256:3cacf757f17d4e7fe6e16f3afe6355c8b2f5415e1d0cde7e5091dfaa8a800c8d","path":"design/implementation-design.md"},{"digest":"sha256:1995fa7ef6862034ba2257cd32b62e3395cdcba44477762d651fc7fd9a5ec32c","path":"design/test-design.md"},{"digest":"sha256:fe8f40803a256b5b65c97f5f4cae862fd55b37cb81f2a803c56c3f654c22e9ef","path":"generated/hello-world.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:028073e4cb24bd7444dd15d48b0e16d37df236edf7a003cb3ca26286aca6c585","path":"source/basic-cli.oracle.json"},{"digest":"sha256:ce602ce2cc0fcefaba288623a675a770d11bc14d224b90045aebbe031330172f","path":"source/original-basic-cli.txt"},{"digest":"sha256:f97359de0fe6181e44c334496993b20b82b49cdbbf0b8b66ee18de7eac34a63b","path":"source/witness-contract.md"},{"digest":"sha256:9d02e5fb3f2793e187a7afa673594340a8cb311d6e212cd3b77ba1a764eb43ee","path":"specification/project-conformance.md"},{"digest":"sha256:e940dcf297eab1d9eafe127b93f56a6b43e0133a0015fee8b1a02818c5e4def3","path":"test-execution-plan.json"},{"digest":"sha256:8b55bf3f6324da565a1de9a5186444e36c43f450484463aafc84b65fd9da4613","path":"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:5449c227c7173bb1b812e46e06d3341b1624e832a2a74105f9a109ee201134d4","path":"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs"}],"files":[{"digest":"sha256:3cacf757f17d4e7fe6e16f3afe6355c8b2f5415e1d0cde7e5091dfaa8a800c8d","path":"design/implementation-design.md"},{"digest":"sha256:1995fa7ef6862034ba2257cd32b62e3395cdcba44477762d651fc7fd9a5ec32c","path":"design/test-design.md"},{"digest":"sha256:fe8f40803a256b5b65c97f5f4cae862fd55b37cb81f2a803c56c3f654c22e9ef","path":"generated/hello-world.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:028073e4cb24bd7444dd15d48b0e16d37df236edf7a003cb3ca26286aca6c585","path":"source/basic-cli.oracle.json"},{"digest":"sha256:ce602ce2cc0fcefaba288623a675a770d11bc14d224b90045aebbe031330172f","path":"source/original-basic-cli.txt"},{"digest":"sha256:f97359de0fe6181e44c334496993b20b82b49cdbbf0b8b66ee18de7eac34a63b","path":"source/witness-contract.md"},{"digest":"sha256:9d02e5fb3f2793e187a7afa673594340a8cb311d6e212cd3b77ba1a764eb43ee","path":"specification/project-conformance.md"},{"digest":"sha256:e940dcf297eab1d9eafe127b93f56a6b43e0133a0015fee8b1a02818c5e4def3","path":"test-execution-plan.json"},{"digest":"sha256:8b55bf3f6324da565a1de9a5186444e36c43f450484463aafc84b65fd9da4613","path":"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs"},{"digest":"sha256:5449c227c7173bb1b812e46e06d3341b1624e832a2a74105f9a109ee201134d4","path":"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs"}],"kind":"native","producerActorRef":null,"producerResultRef":null,"resultDigest":"sha256:4fbf98755483b8f9bf0f6bc34c0646ccc367ce1fb55fe6c30824c3096b4c2b2b","resultRef":"result://abiogenesis/4fbf98755483b8f9bf0f6bc34c0646ccc367ce1fb55fe6c30824c3096b4c2b2b"},"purpose":"design","resultDigest":"sha256:4fbf98755483b8f9bf0f6bc34c0646ccc367ce1fb55fe6c30824c3096b4c2b2b","resultRef":"result://abiogenesis/4fbf98755483b8f9bf0f6bc34c0646ccc367ce1fb55fe6c30824c3096b4c2b2b","selectedGraphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5","synthesisResultRef":"result://abiogenesis/3ee588afbda63abb5d1406c30202aad127111ab61e4c2b217f8ec91a194d092d","value":{"changedPaths":["design/implementation-design.md","design/test-design.md","test-execution-plan.json"],"report":{"gaps":["None of the seven obligations is closed. Each of the three new files needs a record of it being written, plus an independent assessment by a different actor/call. My own checks are not acceptance.","complete-original@5 needs all four written files, current recorded runs of both fixed commands, and an independent assessment that consumes them. behavior@5 and revision@5 need the same assessment. Whether the recorded runs (6514754a before the fix, db34d3cf after it) are current and correctly paired is for the runtime to compute; I did not establish it.","Side effect outside the listed paths: writing the design files created the `design/` folder, which did not exist before. No other off-scope writes. The checks I ran locally (both fixed commands, the TAP-format run, the run from /tmp, and the plan check) created no files, but they are not recorded evidence.","The component and UAT tests are identical in mechanics (same spawn, same two checks). Two files each run the real CLI and pass, but the UAT test adds nothing the component test does not check. Strengthening it would require changing a protected test file, which needs a new decision by whoever owns it.","The tests have no timeout of their own. A hanging CLI is stopped only by the execution harness timeout (20000 ms in the recorded runs).","The tests run the CLI with the same Node binary as the test runner, while fixed command 1 finds `node` through PATH. The Node version is not in the recorded evidence; locally it is v24.7.0.","Unknowns carried over from the conformance file: stderr is not constrained, arguments/stdin/other working directories are not specified, and only one macOS host has been tested.","The original's handwritten `test-execution-result.json` is not written, following conformance C-1/C-2. Its meaning is supposed to be carried by recorded command evidence; the assessor must confirm that this substitution is acceptable."],"summary":"I wrote the three missing files in my write scope. No other file was changed. Writing them also created the `design/` folder, which did not exist before. I did not touch the CLI; it was already corrected (sha256 fe8f4080…).\n\n1. **`design/implementation-design.md`** (sha256 3cacf757…). This is the design for the CLI itself, based on `specification/project-conformance.md` (9d02e5fb…).\n   - It defines `generated/hello-world.mjs` as a single file with no imports and one line: `console.log(\"Hello, world!\");`.\n   - It explains why that line produces exactly the required 14 bytes, why a line ending is always a single LF, and why the script must not call `process.exit()` (that can cut off output written to a pipe).\n   - It checks the current file against the design: it matches. It records the history tied to each version of the file: the failing baseline run on the old version (result 6514754a), the one-line fix (e897db22), and the passing run on the current version (db34d3cf). It also says what would make the design out of date.\n   - It names the component test, the UAT test and both fixed commands, and maps every conformance requirement R-01..R-14 to a part of the design.\n\n2. **`design/test-design.md`** (sha256 1995fa7e…). This is the test design.\n   - It states what the CLI must do: exit status 0, and stdout exactly `Hello, world!\\n`.\n   - It checks both supplied tests line by line against the original instructions. Both run the real CLI and use strict equality for the checks.\n   - It lists which faults the tests catch, and cites the baseline run where both tests failed on the missing comma. That shows the tests actually detect a wrong greeting and do not pass by default.\n   - It specifies both fixed commands and how to read the test counts under both reporter formats. It requires a passing test from each file, not just a total of 2 passes, and spells out the original rule: exit 0, passes at least the expected count, and the plan satisfied.\n   - It lists where the tests fall short (R-T1..R-T4).\n\n3. **`test-execution-plan.json`** (sha256 e940dcf2…).\n   - It has the fields the original requires: `command` \"node\", the exact `args`, `expectedTestPassCount` 2, `expectedStdoutMatch` \"fail 0\" (no exact pass count pinned), and `assertedReturnValue` \"Hello, world!\".\n   - It adds: a direct CLI check (`node generated/hello-world.mjs`, exit 0, exact 14-byte stdout and its hash); the two test names that must pass, one per file; a mapping to both fixed command IDs; the acceptance rule; the fields recorded run evidence must contain; the hashes of the input files; and the baseline → fix → current history.\n   - It states that the plan only declares expectations and does not decide which commands run.\n\n**My own checks (informative only, not recorded evidence):**\n- On local Node v24.7.0, command 1 printed exactly the 14 required bytes and exited 0, and command 2 had 2 passes, 0 failures and exit 0.\n- \"fail 0\" appears in both the default and TAP report formats.\n- Running outside the project root gives `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` and exit 1.\n- I applied the plan's acceptance rule to the recorded test output: it accepts the run on the current CLI and rejects the baseline run.\n- The original source, oracle, witness contract, both tests, the CLI and the conformance file all still match their recorded hashes.\n- I created no temporary files; all checks used pipes or in-memory processing."}}},{"actorInvocationRef":"actor-invocation://abiogenesis/32f133cb65c98e3ab700cf826775bd3017151f12673442326b1c978c3fa59389","cCallRef":"c-call:sha256:cadce5063a56cb5e485d04975dd971253b5e9ed060ed97138805688e0b4df25f","fulfillmentEvidence":{"actorInvocationRef":"actor-invocation://abiogenesis/32f133cb65c98e3ab700cf826775bd3017151f12673442326b1c978c3fa59389","assessmentContractRef":"contract://default-library-witness/assessment@5","cCallRef":"c-call:sha256:cadce5063a56cb5e485d04975dd971253b5e9ed060ed97138805688e0b4df25f","commands":[],"contractRef":"contract://abiogenesis/worksite/native-work/observation@5","dependencies":[{"digest":"sha256:3cacf757f17d4e7fe6e16f3afe6355c8b2f5415e1d0cde7e5091dfa