g directory, exit status, stdout/stderr and resulting test\nobservations. A fabricated success file or a native author's report is insufficient.\n\nThe baseline failure is evidence about its exact earlier subject. Current behavior\nmust be proved against the corrected current subject. Preserve the explicit causal\nrelation between them; neither retarget the old failure to new bytes nor discard\nit merely because the correction changed those bytes. Only support whose claim\ndepends on the old bytes remaining current becomes stale. Unaffected work survives.\n\n## Admitted completion and scope\n\nThe consumer declaration must bind the original and case obligations to explicit\nrealization/proof roles and the selected policy before execution. Meaning and\nsufficiency are attributed F_P judgments. Identity, role correspondence,\ncurrentness and completeness of the selected declared policy are computed from\nadmitted facts. Newly admitted obligations remain visible; missing or unknown\nrequired support leaves the parent open. Scalar UAT success cannot replace the\nrequired pairing and coverage relation.\n\nThe independent assessment must consume current actual evidence and examine all\nmandatory selected outcomes, including authored content, verifier adequacy,\nexecution-plan correspondence and the consequential revision. Its actor/call is\ndistinct from the selected author or measurement producer. Parent completion\nrequires that assessment and eligible admitted coverage. Fresh installed Public\nresult and replay must agree on the actual terminal state and evidence lineage.\n\nProtect original source, oracle, this contract, supplied test sources and installed\nassets. Application writes are confined to the CLI and the four absent asset\npaths above. Command evidence retains its separately declared territory. There\nis no package/network dependency for this application. No caller-owned loop,\nout-of-band application edit, solution-specific framework branch, answer repair\